---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Experiment 3.2: Creating a Periodic Table">
    <main class="container mx-auto px-4 py-8">
        <div class="experiment-header">
            <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-center text-blue-700 mb-2">EXPERIMENT 3.2</h1>
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-center text-blue-700 mb-8">CREATING A PERIODIC TABLE</h2>
        </div>

        <section class="mb-8">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-blue-700">PURPOSE:</h3>
            <p class="mb-4">To model Mendeleev's process by attempting to arrange color cards according to their observed properties of color and intensity.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-8">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-blue-700">MATERIALS:</h3>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-8 mb-4">
                <li>Color cards found in the student notebook (You can also find a copy to print on the Book Extra site.)</li>
                <li>Scissors</li>
                <li>Glue or tape</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-8">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-blue-700">QUESTION:</h3>
            <p class="mb-4">Can you form a periodic table with rows and columns showing a repeating change in properties (color) and increasing atomic mass (shade or color intensity)?</p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-8">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-blue-700">BACKGROUND:</h3>
            <p class="mb-4">
                The color of a card represents its properties. For example, you can consider all green color 
                cards to have similar properties. The green color cards will all have different properties from 
                the orange cards (and all other color cards). The shade (intensity) of a color card represents 
                its atomic mass. In other words, a light (lower intensity) green color card represents an 
                element with a lower atomic mass than a dark (higher intensity) green color card.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-8">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-blue-700">PROCEDURE:</h3>
            <ol class="list-decimal pl-8 mb-4">
                <li class="mb-2">
                    Use the interactive simulation below. You will see 24 color cards organized by color families and a periodic table grid with 34 spaces.
                </li>
                <li class="mb-2">
                    <strong>Drag and drop</strong> the color cards from the card container into the periodic table grid. Arrange them in 8 columns following the rainbow pattern: red, orange, yellow, green, teal, blue, indigo, violet. The first row should have only 2 cards (positions 1 and 8).
                </li>
                <li class="mb-2">
                    Within each column, arrange cards by <strong>increasing intensity</strong> (lighter shades at the top, darker shades at the bottom). This represents increasing atomic mass.
                </li>
                <li class="mb-2">
                    Notice that you have <strong>missing elements</strong> - there are 34 grid spaces but only 24 cards. This models Mendeleev's challenge! Predict where the missing elements belong and describe their properties in the form below.
                </li>
                <li class="mb-2">
                    Use the <strong>"Check Arrangement"</strong> button to verify your periodic table follows the correct pattern (same colors in columns, increasing intensity down each column).
                </li>
                <li class="mb-2">
                    <strong>Tip:</strong> Right-click on any card to return it to its original position. Use the "Reset" button to start over if needed.
                </li>
                <li class="mb-2">
                    Complete the form below with your predictions about missing elements and your conclusions about periodic patterns.
                </li>
            </ol>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-8">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-blue-700">CONCLUSION:</h3>
            <p class="mb-4">
                Were your predictions correct? Explain how the periodic table is a good model for 
                predicting unknown elements and their properties.
            </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Interactive Color Card Simulation -->
        <section class="mb-8">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-blue-700">INTERACTIVE SIMULATION:</h3>
            <p class="mb-4">
                Use this interactive simulation to arrange color cards into a periodic table pattern. 
                Drag and drop the color cards to arrange them by color (property) and intensity (atomic mass).
            </p>
            
            <div id="colorCardSimulation" class="border border-gray-300 rounded-lg p-4 bg-gray-50 min-h-[400px] mb-4">
                <div class="flex justify-between mb-4">
                    <button id="resetBtn" class="bg-red-500 text-white px-4 py-2 rounded-lg">Reset Cards</button>
                    <button id="checkBtn" class="bg-green-500 text-white px-4 py-2 rounded-lg">Check Arrangement</button>
                </div>
                
                <div id="periodicTableGrid" style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(8, 1fr); gap: 8px; max-width: 600px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 16px; background-color: #ffffff; border: 2px solid #d1d5db; border-radius: 8px;">
                    <!-- Grid will be populated by JavaScript -->
                </div>
                
                <div id="colorCardContainer" style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(8, 1fr); gap: 8px; margin-top: 16px; padding: 16px; background-color: #f9fafb; border: 1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius: 8px;">
                    <!-- Color cards will be populated by JavaScript -->
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-8">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-blue-700">SUBMIT YOUR WORK</h3>
            <form id="experimentForm" class="bg-gray-100 p-6 rounded-lg">
                <div class="mb-4">
                    <label for="studentName" class="block text-gray-700 font-bold mb-2">Student Name:</label>
                    <input type="text" id="studentName" name="studentName" class="w-full px-3 py-2 border rounded-lg">
                </div>
                
                <div class="mb-4">
                    <label for="studentEmail" class="block text-gray-700 font-bold mb-2">Student Email:</label>
                    <input type="email" id="studentEmail" name="studentEmail" class="w-full px-3 py-2 border rounded-lg">
                </div>
                

                
                <div class="mb-6">
                    <div class="mb-2">
                        <label for="missingElements" class="block text-gray-700 font-bold">Describe your predictions for the missing elements:</label>
                    </div>
                    <textarea id="missingElements" name="missingElements" rows="6" class="w-full px-3 py-2 border rounded-lg resize-y" placeholder="Based on the patterns you observed in the periodic table simulation, what properties do you predict for the missing elements? Consider their position, color family, and expected intensity."></textarea>
                </div>
                
                <div class="mb-6">
                    <div class="mb-2">
                        <label for="conclusion" class="block text-gray-700 font-bold">Conclusion:</label>
                    </div>
                    <textarea id="conclusion" name="conclusion" rows="10" class="w-full px-3 py-2 border rounded-lg resize-y" placeholder="Were your predictions correct? Explain how the periodic table is a good model for predicting unknown elements and their properties. What patterns did you discover?"></textarea>
                </div>
                
                <div class="flex justify-end">
                    <button type="submit" class="bg-blue-600 text-white px-6 py-2 rounded-lg hover:bg-blue-700">Submit Experiment</button>
                </div>
            </form>
        </section>

        <div class="mt-8 text-center">
            <a href="/physical-science" class="inline-block bg-blue-600 text-white px-6 py-2 rounded-lg hover:bg-blue-700">Back to Physical Science</a>
        </div>
    </main>

    <!-- EmailJS CDN -->
    <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@emailjs/browser@3/dist/email.min.js"></script>
    
    <script>
        // Wait for DOM to be fully loaded
        document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function() {
            console.log('DOM loaded, starting simulation setup...');
            
            // Color card data
            const colors = ['red', 'orange', 'yellow', 'green', 'teal', 'blue', 'indigo', 'violet'];
            const intensities = ['100', '300', '500', '700', '900']; // Tailwind color intensities
            
            // Create the periodic table grid
            const grid = document.getElementById('periodicTableGrid');
            console.log('Grid element:', grid);
            if (!grid) {
                console.error('Grid element not found!');
                return;
            }
            
            for (let row = 0; row < 5; row++) {
                for (let col = 0; col < 8; col++) {
                    // First row only has 2 elements (positions 0 and 7)
                    if (row === 0 && col > 0 && col < 7) {
                        const emptyCell = document.createElement('div');
                        emptyCell.className = 'h-16 w-16 border border-dashed border-gray-300 rounded bg-gray-100';
                        emptyCell.style.cssText = 'width: 64px; height: 64px; border: 2px dashed #d1d5db; background-color: #f3f4f6; border-radius: 8px; display: block;';
                        grid.appendChild(emptyCell);
                    } else {
                        const cell = document.createElement('div');
                        cell.className = 'h-16 w-16 border border-gray-300 rounded droppable bg-white hover:bg-gray-50';
                        cell.style.cssText = 'width: 64px; height: 64px; border: 2px solid #d1d5db; background-color: white; border-radius: 8px; display: block;';
                        cell.dataset.row = row;
                        cell.dataset.col = col;
                        
                        // Add the ID that the chart generation function expects
                        const cellIndex = row * 8 + col;
                        cell.id = 'cell-' + cellIndex;
                    cell.addEventListener('dragover', (e) => {
                        e.preventDefault();
                        cell.classList.add('border-blue-500');
                    });
                    cell.addEventListener('dragleave', () => {
                        cell.classList.remove('border-blue-500');
                    });
                    cell.addEventListener('drop', (e) => {
                        e.preventDefault();
                        cell.classList.remove('border-blue-500');
                        const cardId = e.dataTransfer.getData('text/plain');
                        const card = document.getElementById(cardId);
                        
                        // Enhanced drop logic: handle occupied cells
                        if (cell.children.length === 0) {
                            cell.appendChild(card);
                        } else {
                            // If cell is occupied, return card to original slot
                            const originalSlotIndex = card.dataset.originalSlot;
                            const originalSlot = document.getElementById(`slot-${originalSlotIndex}`);
                            if (originalSlot) {
                                originalSlot.appendChild(card);
                            }
                        }
                        });
                        grid.appendChild(cell);
                    }
                }
            }
            
            console.log('Grid creation completed, grid has', grid.children.length, 'cells');
            
            // Create the color cards
            const cardContainer = document.getElementById('colorCardContainer');
            console.log('Card container element:', cardContainer);
            if (!cardContainer) {
                console.error('Card container element not found!');
                return;
            }
            
            let cardId = 1;
            
            // Create cards organized in columns by color families (like periodic table)
            // Each column will be a color family, each row will be an intensity level
            const availableCards = [];
            
            // Build cards by intensity first, then by color (to create column arrangement)
            const intensityLevels = ['100', '500', '900'];
            const colorFamilies = ['red', 'orange', 'yellow', 'green', 'teal', 'blue', 'indigo', 'violet'];
            
            // Create cards in column order: all light colors first, then medium, then dark
            intensityLevels.forEach(intensity => {
                colorFamilies.forEach(color => {
                    availableCards.push({color: color, intensity: intensity});
                });
            });
            
            // Keep cards organized (don't shuffle) to show the pattern clearly
            const shuffledCards = availableCards;
            
            // First, create placeholder slots for all 24 positions to maintain grid structure
            for (let i = 0; i < 24; i++) {
                const slot = document.createElement('div');
                slot.id = `slot-${i}`;
                slot.className = 'card-slot';
                slot.style.cssText = 'width: 48px; height: 48px; border: 2px dashed #d1d5db; border-radius: 8px; display: block; justify-self: center; align-self: center; background-color: #f9fafb;';
                cardContainer.appendChild(slot);
            }
            
            // Create the card elements and place them in their slots
            console.log('Creating', shuffledCards.length, 'color cards...');
            shuffledCards.forEach((cardData, index) => {
                const card = document.createElement('div');
                card.id = `card-${cardId++}`;
                card.className = `w-12 h-12 bg-${cardData.color}-${cardData.intensity} rounded cursor-move draggable`;
                
                // Add inline styles to ensure visibility
                const colorMap = {
                    'red': {'100': '#fee2e2', '300': '#fca5a5', '500': '#ef4444', '700': '#b91c1c', '900': '#7f1d1d'},
                    'orange': {'100': '#fed7aa', '300': '#fdba74', '500': '#f97316', '700': '#c2410c', '900': '#7c2d12'},
                    'yellow': {'100': '#fef3c7', '300': '#fcd34d', '500': '#eab308', '700': '#a16207', '900': '#713f12'},
                    'green': {'100': '#dcfce7', '300': '#86efac', '500': '#22c55e', '700': '#15803d', '900': '#14532d'},
                    'teal': {'100': '#ccfbf1', '300': '#5eead4', '500': '#14b8a6', '700': '#0f766e', '900': '#134e4a'},
                    'blue': {'100': '#dbeafe', '300': '#93c5fd', '500': '#3b82f6', '700': '#1d4ed8', '900': '#1e3a8a'},
                    'indigo': {'100': '#e0e7ff', '300': '#a5b4fc', '500': '#6366f1', '700': '#4338ca', '900': '#312e81'},
                    'violet': {'100': '#ede9fe', '300': '#c4b5fd', '500': '#8b5cf6', '700': '#6d28d9', '900': '#4c1d95'}
                };
                
                const bgColor = colorMap[cardData.color][cardData.intensity] || '#gray';
                card.style.cssText = `width: 48px; height: 48px; background-color: ${bgColor}; border-radius: 8px; cursor: move; display: block; position: absolute; z-index: 10;`;
                card.draggable = true;
                card.dataset.color = cardData.color;
                card.dataset.intensity = cardData.intensity;
                card.dataset.originalSlot = index; // Remember original position
                
                card.addEventListener('dragstart', (e) => {
                    e.dataTransfer.setData('text/plain', card.id);
                });
                
                // Add right-click to remove functionality
                card.addEventListener('contextmenu', (e) => {
                    e.preventDefault(); // Prevent browser context menu
                    
                    // Return card to its original slot (enhanced logic)
                    const originalSlotIndex = card.dataset.originalSlot;
                    const originalSlot = document.getElementById(`slot-${originalSlotIndex}`);
                    if (originalSlot && originalSlot.children.length === 0) {
                        originalSlot.appendChild(card);
                    } else if (originalSlot && originalSlot.children.length > 0) {
                        // If original slot is occupied, swap cards
                        const occupyingCard = originalSlot.firstChild;
                        const currentParent = card.parentNode;
                        if (currentParent && currentParent.classList.contains('droppable')) {
                            currentParent.appendChild(occupyingCard);
                        }
                        originalSlot.appendChild(card);
                    }
                });
                
                // Place card in its corresponding slot
                const slot = document.getElementById(`slot-${index}`);
                slot.style.position = 'relative';
                slot.appendChild(card);
            });
            console.log('Card creation completed, container has', cardContainer.children.length, 'cards');
            
            // Reset button functionality
            document.getElementById('resetBtn').addEventListener('click', () => {
                const cards = document.querySelectorAll('.draggable');
                cards.forEach(card => {
                    const originalSlotIndex = card.dataset.originalSlot;
                    const originalSlot = document.getElementById(`slot-${originalSlotIndex}`);
                    if (originalSlot) {
                        originalSlot.appendChild(card);
                    }
                });
            });
            
            // Check arrangement button - improved validation
            document.getElementById('checkBtn').addEventListener('click', () => {
                let correct = true;
                let feedback = [];
                const filledCells = document.querySelectorAll('.droppable:not(:empty)');
                
                if (filledCells.length === 0) {
                    alert('Try placing some cards in the periodic table grid first!');
                    return;
                }
                
                // Group cards by column to check color consistency
                const columnGroups = {};
                
                filledCells.forEach(cell => {
                    const row = parseInt(cell.dataset.row);
                    const col = parseInt(cell.dataset.col);
                    const card = cell.firstChild;
                    const cardColor = card.dataset.color;
                    const cardIntensity = card.dataset.intensity;
                    
                    if (!columnGroups[col]) {
                        columnGroups[col] = [];
                    }
                    columnGroups[col].push({row, color: cardColor, intensity: cardIntensity});
                });
                
                // Check each column for color consistency and intensity progression
                Object.keys(columnGroups).forEach(col => {
                    const columnCards = columnGroups[col];
                    
                    // Check if all cards in column have same color
                    const firstColor = columnCards[0].color;
                    const allSameColor = columnCards.every(card => card.color === firstColor);
                    if (!allSameColor) {
                        correct = false;
                        feedback.push(`Column ${parseInt(col) + 1} has mixed colors - should all be the same color family.`);
                    }
                    
                    // Check if intensity increases down the column
                    columnCards.sort((a, b) => a.row - b.row);
                    for (let i = 1; i < columnCards.length; i++) {
                        const prevIntensity = parseInt(columnCards[i-1].intensity);
                        const currIntensity = parseInt(columnCards[i].intensity);
                        if (currIntensity <= prevIntensity) {
                            correct = false;
                            feedback.push(`Column ${parseInt(col) + 1} intensity should increase going down.`);
                            break;
                        }
                    }
                });
                
                if (correct) {
                    alert('Excellent work! Your periodic table arrangement follows the correct pattern: same colors in columns and increasing intensity down each column!');
                } else {
                    let feedbackMsg;
                    if (feedback.length > 0) {
                        feedbackMsg = 'Good effort! Here are some tips:\n• ' + feedback.join('\n• ') + 
                            '\n\nRemember: columns should have the same color (property) and intensity should increase going down each column.';
                    } else {
                        feedbackMsg = 'Not quite right. Remember: columns should have the same color (property) and intensity (atomic mass) should increase as you go down each column.';
                    }
                    alert(feedbackMsg);
                }
            });
            
            // Initialize EmailJS
            emailjs.init('ct_s19oZHppLy9BlW');
            
            // Form submission
            document.getElementById('experimentForm').addEventListener('submit', function(e) {
                e.preventDefault();
                
                const studentName = document.getElementById('studentName').value;
                const studentEmail = document.getElementById('studentEmail').value;
                const missingElements = document.getElementById('missingElements').value;
                const conclusion = document.getElementById('conclusion').value;
                
                // Enhanced form validation for all required fields
                if (!studentName || !studentEmail || !missingElements || !conclusion) {
                    alert('Please fill in all required fields: name, email, missing elements predictions, and conclusion.');
                    return;
                }
                
                // Function to capture current periodic table arrangement
                function capturePeriodicTable() {
                    let tableRepresentation = '\nSTUDENT\'S PERIODIC TABLE ARRANGEMENT:\n';
                    tableRepresentation += '=' .repeat(50) + '\n';
                    
                    // Create 5 rows x 8 columns representation
                    for (let row = 0; row < 5; row++) {
                        let rowText = '';
                        for (let col = 0; col < 8; col++) {
                            const cellIndex = row * 8 + col;
                            const cell = document.getElementById('cell-' + cellIndex);
                            
                            if (cell && cell.children.length > 0) {
                                const card = cell.children[0];
                                const color = card.dataset.color || 'unknown';
                                const intensity = card.dataset.intensity || '?';
                                rowText += '[' + color.substring(0,3).toUpperCase() + intensity + '] ';
                            } else if ((row === 0 && col !== 0 && col !== 7) || 
                                     (row === 1 && (col === 1 || col === 6))) {
                                // Skip positions that should be empty in first two rows
                                rowText += '       ';
                            } else {
                                rowText += '[EMPTY] ';
                            }
                        }
                        tableRepresentation += rowText + '\n';
                    }
                    
                    tableRepresentation += '=' .repeat(50) + '\n';
                    tableRepresentation += 'Legend: [COLOR+INTENSITY] - RED100, ORG300, etc.\n';
                    tableRepresentation += 'EMPTY = Missing element (student prediction needed)\n\n';
                    
                    return tableRepresentation;
                }
                
                // Prepare experiment data for email
                const periodicTableChart = capturePeriodicTable();
                const experimentData = 'EXPERIMENT 3.2: CREATING A PERIODIC TABLE\n\n' +
                    'Student: ' + studentName + '\n' +
                    'Email: ' + studentEmail + '\n\n' +
                    periodicTableChart +
                    'MISSING ELEMENTS PREDICTIONS:\n' + missingElements + '\n\n' +
                    'CONCLUSION:\n' + conclusion + '\n\n' +
                    'Experiment completed: ' + new Date().toLocaleString();
                
                // Send email using EmailJS
                emailjs.send('service_ot1jg6s', 'template_y556rhr', {
                    student_name: studentName,
                    student_email: studentEmail,
                    experiment_title: 'Experiment 3.2: Creating a Periodic Table',
                    hypothesis: 'See periodic table arrangement and predictions below',
                    missing_elements: missingElements,
                    conclusion: experimentData,
                    subject: `Experiment 3.2 - ${studentName}`
                }).then(function(response) {
                    console.log('SUCCESS!', response.status, response.text);
                    alert('Your experiment has been submitted successfully! Your teacher will be notified.');
                    document.getElementById('experimentForm').reset();
                }, function(error) {
                    console.log('FAILED...', error);
                    alert('Failed to submit. Please try again.');
                });
            });
            
        }); // Close DOMContentLoaded
    </script>
</Layout>
